1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,040
THE CHARACTERS, RACES,
AND LOCATIONS ARE FICTIONAL.

2
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:12,720
THE HISTORY OF MINORITY STRUGGLES IS REAL.

3
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,600
Here it comes.

4
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,040
<i>My child, your name will be Naka.</i>

5
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:51,520
<i>after our sacred mountain range.</i>

6
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,840
Mothulas…

7
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:55,920
Stop it.

8
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,480
-Why don't you go inside?
-Let go!

9
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,160
-I'll kill every last Savin!
-No!

10
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,080
-Siprai, stop!
-Ongdee!

11
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,200
What the hell did you just do?

12
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,760
He's Savin.

13
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,320
<i>It couldn't be anyone but Prapt.</i>

14
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,680
IF YOU DON'T DUMP THAT CAPTAIN,
I'LL KILL HIM.

15
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,840
I won't let Chart get hurt because of me.

16
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:13,400
We should tell Chart.

17
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:28,760
<i>Mom, exam season is approaching.</i>

18
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,360
<i>Siprai and I have to study harder.</i>

19
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,200
<i>Studying here is tougher than I thought,</i>

20
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:37,600
<i>maybe because we've been away</i>
<i>from school for so long.</i>

21
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:40,360
<i>"But I will try my absolute best</i>

22
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:44,480
so these four years go smoothly,

23
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,240
and I can return

24
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:49,640
to hug you as much as I miss you."

25
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:03,080
<i>I still think of our Kase land</i>
<i>with every breath.</i>

26
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:06,240
<i>I want to return and fight</i>
<i>alongside our Kase warriors.</i>

27
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,240
<i>"And I want to rest</i>
<i>my head on your lap again</i>

28
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,960
more than anything."

29
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:11,880
"Love you with all my heart,

30
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,880
Mintada."

31
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,760
Send my love to Khengla,

32
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:21,160
my second love after mother.

33
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:22,720
Mintada.

34
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,200
Khengla, where does it say that?

35
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,600
Right here, Yiaza.
Here, let me read it to you.

36
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,960
"Khengla, Manu,

37
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,040
please take care of my mother."

38
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,880
Manu, what are you laughing at?

39
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,680
Mintada didn't write your name,

40
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,280
I added it out of pity
for someone with no hope.

41
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,760
Thanks but no thanks for next time.

42
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:51,080
-Really?
-Hey.

43
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,640
Give it here.

44
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:53,920
Stop teasing Manu, Khengla.

45
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,560
Oh, dear! Give that letter here.

46
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,600
Mintada wrote that for me.

47
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,760
Sa. Nee.

48
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,080
Sa, Nee, have you seen this?

49
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,880
Calling all forest lovers.

50
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:12,800
Yeah. School's out and off we go!
Let's go.

51
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:14,800
Yep, we will. Shall we?

52
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,839
Sa, wait… Why that face of backing out?

53
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,440
You can't.

54
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:21,720
You dragged us into this club, remember?

55
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,880
I'm just not sure
if my parents will let me go.

56
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:26,600
Of course they will.

57
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,840
We'll help persuade them.

58
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,440
Exactly. Nothing to be afraid of.

59
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:33,040
We're going as a group,
several professors are coming,

60
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,720
and park rangers will be watching
over us the whole time.

61
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,040
-Come on.
-Please.

62
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,480
-Let's go together.
-Sa.

63
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,560
-Sa, please go.
-Pretty please.

64
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:46,160
-Please, please, please.
-Fine.

65
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,840
Yay. So it's settled, you're going.

66
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,080
Not yet.

67
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:51,480
I need to ask my parents first.

68
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:55,680
Too late. I already signed us up.
All that's left is paying for three seats.

69
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,160
-Let's get food, Nee.
-Yeah.

70
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:02,440
Yoon. Nee. I haven't promised yet.

71
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,120
Here.

72
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:22,240
Thank you.

73
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:35,320
Being out in nature is so refreshing.

74
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:41,640
Thank you so much for bringing me here.

75
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,920
You work hard. You need
to rest sometimes, you know?

76
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:50,440
Yes, Sir. Let's sit and rest.

77
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,800
Look, the water is so clear.

78
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:06,400
Wait. Can I have a sip?

79
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:10,320
No. No sharing drinks.

80
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,880
Everyone keeps their own.

81
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:14,440
Safety and hygiene first.

82
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:18,080
I don't get sick easily.
I'm strong as a horse.

83
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,840
See how fit I am? Let me have a sip.

84
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:23,320
No. This is mine. Yours is right there.

85
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,240
I want this one.

86
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,040
-No. No.
-Just a little bit.

87
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,840
-Just a tiny bit.
-Chart.

88
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,040
Just a little bit, please?

89
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,160
-No.
-Just a little.

90
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,240
-Chart.
-Just a sip.

91
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,880
-Just a little bit.
-Chart.

92
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,200
Fine.

93
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,680
-Chart.
-It's okay.

94
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,680
Serves you right.

95
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:48,920
Wait here a moment. I'll be right back.

96
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:02,800
Irene.

97
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:04,920
Irene.

98
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,000
Irene.

99
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:16,880
Irene.

100
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,160
Irene.

101
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,800
Irene, what are you doing?

102
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,920
I came to get water to wash you up.

103
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,120
But I have a better idea.

104
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,560
What is it?

105
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,960
Chart…

106
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:26,920
Hey.

107
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,520
You're the one who made me messy.
You have to help me wash off.

108
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,840
Look, I'm covered in it.

109
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:33,919
-Come on.
-No.

110
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:36,520
-Are you coming or not?
-No.

111
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,280
-Help me now.
-Chart…

112
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:40,200
I'm messy all over, look.

113
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,360
No.

114
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:43,919
-Now.
-Chart.

115
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:44,840
-Come on.
-Chart, stop.

116
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,600
llDon't. I'm getting wet.

117
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,960
-Come.
-Chart, I'm soaked.

118
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,560
Hey, Chart!

119
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,120
-Here!
-Whoa!

120
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,520
-Take this.
-It's cold.

121
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:11,960
Stop it.

122
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,200
Here.

123
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,160
Enough!

124
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,480
Eat this.

125
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,240
I'll fight back!

126
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,440
I said just a moment.

127
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,320
Let me finish this song.

128
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,160
-We're sorry.
-Sorry.

129
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,920
<i>Brothers and sisters</i>

130
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:01,560
<i>We eat fish, we protect the stream</i>
<i>Protect it, yes, protect it</i>

131
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:07,040
<i>We eat frogs, we guard the cliff</i>
<i>Guard the cliff, yes, guard the cliff</i>

132
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:09,280
<i>Do not admire…</i>

133
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:21,480
Hey.

134
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,760
Still not well?

135
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,960
What? I'm not sick.

136
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:34,440
I've been through this before.

137
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:37,080
It's no different from being possessed.

138
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,880
Once it hits, it's hard to cure.

139
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:41,840
But as an experienced guy,
I'm telling you,

140
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,440
don't let your mind wander.

141
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:46,280
Or you'll fail your exam.

142
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,280
Yeah.

143
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,400
Where's Ongdee?

144
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,720
I'm here.

145
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,200
Ready, everyone?

146
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,240
-Ready.
-Ready.

147
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,920
Come on.

148
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,760
Let's start.

149
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:04,880
Question number one.

150
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,280
Read along, "For what reason…"

151
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:13,160
-Read along.
-"For what reason…"

152
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,280
Wow. Smells so good.

153
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:21,920
Here.

154
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:23,800
For you.

155
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,640
-Try it.
-Okay.

156
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:37,880
How is it?

157
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,720
The canned fish tastes so good.

158
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,520
Wait, isn't it because of the cook?

159
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,920
-I seasoned it well.
-It's really good.

160
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,400
-Yummy?
-I mean the canned fish.

161
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,240
It's really good.

162
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,040
It's like--

163
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,960
Pretty romantic, right?
Dining in the rain.

164
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,200
Be romantic alone.

165
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,680
-I'm heading inside.
-Oh, wait.

166
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,760
Since we're soaked,
we should take off our shirts.

167
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,520
Or we'll get pneumonia.

168
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:45,840
You're a nurse, so you of all people know.
Don't be stubborn.

169
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:35,880
Mintada.

170
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:39,040
What?

171
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,200
What are you doing, student?

172
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:48,600
Nothing, Ma'am.

173
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:52,280
Nothing? I just saw you
holding up two fingers like this.

174
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:58,360
Two fingers means…
Encouragement for everyone.

175
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:04,920
Get back to your test.
It isn't the time to give encouragement.

176
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,480
Continue your test.

177
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:11,840
Don't let me catch you again
or I'll kick you both out of the room.

178
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:14,120
-Yes, Ma'am.
-Yes, Ma'am.

179
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,880
How'd it go? How was the test?

180
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:40,720
At my level, failing isn't an option.

181
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:43,600
My brain is about to explode, though.

182
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,640
What about you, Mintada?

183
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:49,280
I managed, but luckily you helped.

184
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:50,440
I'd be toast without you.

185
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:54,920
It's on you too. You worked hard.
That's why you pulled it off.

186
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:59,560
But I'm done. I need to sleep.

187
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,080
Siprai.

188
00:17:04,839 --> 00:17:06,280
Definitely out for the count.

189
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,839
What are you reading, Ongdee?

190
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,280
An acceptance letter

191
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,839
from the Savin Student Council.

192
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:25,319
They want me to be the president
of Savin students in Thailand.

193
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:26,960
Congrats, Ongdee!

194
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,800
It's not about the position.

195
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:32,000
I'm glad I can take care of us,

196
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,000
not just the Savin,

197
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:37,440
but every ethnic group born on Savin soil.

198
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,160
You're truly a good person.

199
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,360
-Hurry up!
-Quick!

200
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,200
I'm so excited.

201
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:05,480
I'm coming.

202
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:08,800
-The exam results are out.
-Let's look together.

203
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:12,120
-One, two, three!
-Two, three!

204
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,800
Wow, 3.2. Hooray!

205
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:22,920
It's okay, Yoon.
You can try again next term.

206
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,280
Try again for what? I…

207
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,000
I got 3.5!

208
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:33,560
-Sorry.
-Sorry.

209
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,760
Hey, Yoon. You got higher than me.

210
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:38,160
You acted sad for nothing.

211
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,920
Sa, let me see yours.

212
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,520
It's really not that much.

213
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:44,920
3.7!

214
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:49,600
-Am I the lowest one here?
-Not at all.

215
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:53,160
Look, I made a deal with my dad.
If I hit 3.5,

216
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,920
I could join your forest trip.

217
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,680
That means you get to come with us then.

218
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,400
I hope so.

219
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:02,560
-What now?
-You know how my dad is.

220
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:07,160
If I were you, I'd sit
right in front of the house, no eating,

221
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:10,880
no sleeping, no doing anything
until he gives in!

222
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,120
-Yoon!
-Yoon.

223
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:17,000
-We're getting looks.
-Alright, alright.

224
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:19,000
Calm down. Forget it!

225
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:21,840
Let's go grab something nice

226
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:22,760
-and celebrate.
-Yeah!

227
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:25,120
-Let's go!
-Yoon, look at your speed.

228
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,240
I'm not rushing at all!
Not even a little bit.

229
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:29,400
Weren't you just threatening
to starve yourself.

230
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,840
Well, I got 3.5.

231
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:34,360
Huh? That's all I got.

232
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:46,160
Better than an F.

233
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:48,120
Man, I wanna quit.

234
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:52,520
I'd rather head back to Kase
and fight the Savins and Mothulas.

235
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:53,760
No, you can't.

236
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:56,000
Why?

237
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:00,040
We promised Colonel Layee

238
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:04,160
that we would return to embrace
Kase land once again, holding our degrees.

239
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:06,840
So no going home for four years straight?

240
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:08,960
Yes.

241
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,160
I miss home terribly too.

242
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,240
But we must endure

243
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:18,720
for the future of all Kases.

244
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:36,680
So, Lady Punpussa.
Can you tell us if you're coming or not?

245
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,600
That way we'll know
if we're an even or odd group.

246
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:44,280
Even or odd? Wouldn't it be simpler
to just say two or three?

247
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:49,080
-So what's your answer?
-Relax.

248
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:51,640
I'll find the right time to ask him.

249
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,960
When is that right time ever coming?

250
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,040
Your dad's barely ever home.

251
00:20:57,120 --> 00:20:59,360
He's always away inspecting projects.

252
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:02,560
By then, we'll have gone and come back.

253
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:07,560
Look at you! Getting permission
for a trip is like going to war.

254
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:09,200
Why is he so overprotective?

255
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:12,080
Oh, please. Lady Punpussa

256
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:16,200
is their beloved precious only child.

257
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:17,600
Alright, enough.

258
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:21,320
How about this,
what if we talk to him for you?

259
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:24,160
Absolutely not.
Stop right there, both of you.

260
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,720
I'll take care of it myself.

261
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,920
Are you sure you can handle it?

262
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,960
Just trust me.

263
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,080
We can't go back to Kase during a break.

264
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:39,520
So what are we going to do
for all these months?

265
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,720
I'm taking summer classes.
Knock out credits.

266
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:43,680
So we graduate and go home sooner.

267
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:48,200
Man, it's break time!
Instead of resting, you wanna study more?

268
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:51,840
If you want a break, there's plenty
of time before the summer semester starts.

269
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,040
Tell you what.

270
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,840
How about we go on a trip?

271
00:21:56,760 --> 00:21:57,600
Hell yeah, I'm down!

272
00:21:58,800 --> 00:21:59,920
I'd rather not.

273
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:01,560
Why not, Mintada?

274
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:03,320
Don't you want to explore Thailand?

275
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:06,400
This country has so many beautiful places.

276
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:11,240
The money we receive
is a scholarship provided by the Union.

277
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,320
We shouldn't be spending it wastefully.

278
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:16,640
Trust me.
This trip will cost almost nothing.

279
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:20,000
My friend offered to drive us around.

280
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:22,480
We'll keep it simple,
eating light and sleeping in tents.

281
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,800
Come on, Mintada.

282
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:27,400
-What's wrong with you?
-Right.

283
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:28,840
Once in a lifetime.

284
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:32,520
Fine. Count me in.

285
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:37,760
Whoa!

286
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:39,840
Every man for himself. Run!

287
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:50,360
-I thought the rainy season was over!
-Must be a summer storm.

288
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,200
-Oh, no.
-No.

289
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,480
It's raining!

290
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:59,520
Look, Sa! You have to come with us.

291
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:01,880
I don't want to be stuck with Yoon alone.

292
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:08,200
Hey! As if I wanna be stuck with you.

293
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:09,920
Here we go again.

294
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:12,800
Forget about Khao Yai for a second.

295
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,520
How are we even leaving right now?

296
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,840
It's pouring!

297
00:23:15,920 --> 00:23:17,800
Don't touch me.

298
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:49,160
I'm not superstitious.
Just trying it for fun, for encouragement.

299
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:53,280
Go for it. But I want you to know

300
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:56,560
that one thing
we humans have and it's strong

301
00:23:57,360 --> 00:23:58,360
is a heart.

302
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,280
Whatever you do,

303
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:03,600
I want you to trust your heart.

304
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:08,520
Can I trust your heart too?

305
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,640
I'm a man you can trust for life.

306
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:41,800
-Come on. Get in.
-Hey.

307
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:44,160
Why hasn't Sa shown up yet?

308
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:45,160
Right?

309
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:48,200
Maybe her parents didn't let her come.

310
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:49,840
Really?

311
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:51,840
I don't know. Let me call her first.

312
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:53,520
-I'll go call Sa. Wait here.
-Yoon!

313
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:56,120
What are you waiting for?
Get in the van. Let's go.

314
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:58,960
-We're pulling out now. Quick.
-What now?

315
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,600
It's like this every time.

316
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:03,200
-Let's go.
-Come on.

317
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:05,160
-Board please.
-Yoon, Nee.

318
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,520
-Sa!
-Hey, Sa!

319
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:11,520
-Sa.
-Thought you weren't coming!

320
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:15,480
I almost didn't. I had to beg
my dad forever before he finally gave in.

321
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,880
Tell us on the van. Get in, fast!

322
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:20,040
-Come on.
-Hello, Ma'am.

323
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:21,560
-Hello.
-Go, go.

324
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:23,680
-Well done, Sa.
-All here?

325
00:25:23,760 --> 00:25:24,840
Yes, Ma'am.

326
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:27,520
Move it. Load the bags.

327
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:31,360
Come on, everyone.

328
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:33,480
Tarsh Tour is ready to roll. Let's go.

329
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:34,600
Let's go.

330
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:36,800
-Siprai…
-Hey.

331
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,760
What about Siprai? Where is he?

332
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:40,240
-I'll go grab him.
-Go.

333
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:41,680
Siprai is coming!

334
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:45,200
Here I am! Go!

335
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:47,280
-Go. Let's go! Hop on.
-Wow.

336
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:48,200
-Come on, man!
-Slick move.

337
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:49,160
Let's go.

338
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:51,800
-Let's move.
-Ongdee.

339
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:53,240
Why not take the front seat?

340
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:55,680
Back here is better.
I get to sit with everyone.

341
00:25:56,280 --> 00:25:57,200
Come.

342
00:25:58,480 --> 00:26:01,120
Go. We're rolling out!

343
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:03,040
We're ready.

344
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:07,680
Here we go.

345
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:10,680
Move it! Move it!

346
00:26:10,760 --> 00:26:12,440
Welcome, professors

347
00:26:12,520 --> 00:26:15,320
and nature-loving students.

348
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:18,120
You may have hiked before.

349
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:20,640
But I believe this trip

350
00:26:20,720 --> 00:26:22,400
will be completely different.

351
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:24,280
From this moment on,

352
00:26:24,360 --> 00:26:26,800
let's talk less,

353
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:29,080
and open our eyes and ears wider

354
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:31,240
to truly feel nature

355
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:33,680
in all its diversity.

356
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:35,600
I believe this experience

357
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:38,320
might just change your lives.

358
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:41,280
Are you ready?

359
00:26:41,360 --> 00:26:42,800
Yes!

360
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:52,360
Keep together, everyone.

361
00:26:53,840 --> 00:26:56,480
This area is tropical rainforest.

362
00:26:56,560 --> 00:27:00,760
As for wildlife, we have gibbons,
hornbills, oriental pied hornbills.

363
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:02,920
Also squirrels.

364
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:05,600
Follow me. Come along.

365
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:17,760
When are we gonna get there?

366
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:21,560
How many batteries
did Lady Punpussa put in today?

367
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:22,640
Still full of energy.

368
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:27,480
I thought she wouldn't make it.
But we're the ones struggling.

369
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:31,200
Oh, right. Let's take
a quick energy boost then.

370
00:27:31,280 --> 00:27:32,800
-Yes, sure.
-Here I got--

371
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:34,560
-Hey, they're moving!
-Share some.

372
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:36,800
-Sa, come on.
-Lemme get a bite.

373
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:38,040
Sa, follow us.

374
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,400
-Taste real good.
-Yum.

375
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:10,520
-We're here.
-Okay.

376
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:26,000
How is it? Is this forest like Kase?

377
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:30,520
Ours is much more pristine
like I told you.

378
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:33,000
We Kase people revere trees.

379
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:35,400
We'd never let anyone harm our forest.

380
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:37,680
Unlike people here.

381
00:28:38,840 --> 00:28:39,800
How so?

382
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:42,920
Everyone tries to exploit the forest

383
00:28:43,520 --> 00:28:46,480
without caring if there'll be
anything left for the future.

384
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:51,280
Such a waste. Blessed with good things,
yet they don't protect them.

385
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:52,920
Exactly.

386
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:26,280
Yoon. Nee. Where are you?

387
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:28,080
Yoon! Nee!

388
00:29:28,760 --> 00:29:30,000
I'm here.

389
00:29:30,080 --> 00:29:32,720
Yoon! Nee!

390
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:53,440
Yoon. Nee.

391
00:29:57,640 --> 00:30:00,680
We'll camp here tonight.
Let's go grab some food first.

392
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:03,240
Great. Time for some nostalgia.

393
00:30:03,320 --> 00:30:05,360
I haven't scavenged for wild food in ages.

394
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:07,360
Hey, hold it right there! You can't.

395
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:10,560
This isn't back home.
It's forbidden. Go buy food.

396
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:13,600
Buy food? We're in the woods
and still gotta buy food?

397
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,920
Yeah, come on, you two!

398
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,240
Come.

399
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:18,240
What the heck?

400
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:35,760
BEWARE OF WILD ELEPHANTS

401
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:52,320
That wraps up our first day of hiking.

402
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:55,000
Give yourselves a round of applause.

403
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,440
Are we there already?

404
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:07,360
-How's it going?
-You said first day.

405
00:31:07,440 --> 00:31:10,080
Does that mean
there's a day two and three?

406
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:12,760
Yes. Today was just two kilometers.

407
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:16,200
-Time was short, think of it as a warm-up.
-Huh?

408
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:18,240
Tomorrow we'll go much further.

409
00:31:18,320 --> 00:31:20,440
-Huh?
-And it'll be way more fun.

410
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:22,760
Fun?

411
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:24,960
Fun how? More like torture.

412
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:28,040
Alright. Head off and rest.

413
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:30,600
We have more planned for tonight.

414
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:36,800
-Sa?
-Sa? Where's Sa?

415
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:38,720
-Excuse me, Sir!
-Yes.

416
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:42,320
-What's wrong?
-Our friend is missing!

417
00:32:18,120 --> 00:32:19,080
Help me!

418
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:22,960
Help!

419
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:27,920
Do you remember
where you last saw Punpussa?

420
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:30,880
I'm not sure, Professor.

421
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:33,200
By the time we realized,
Sa was already gone.

422
00:32:33,280 --> 00:32:35,880
Spread out and search now

423
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:37,400
before it gets dark.

424
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:40,240
Report back immediately
if you find any tracks or clues.

425
00:32:40,320 --> 00:32:42,240
-Move out!
-Yes, Sir.

426
00:32:51,520 --> 00:32:53,680
Yoon, what happened?

427
00:32:53,760 --> 00:32:56,520
We were doing forest activities.

428
00:32:57,320 --> 00:33:00,240
When we got back, Punpussa was gone.

429
00:33:00,320 --> 00:33:02,800
-Is she lost in the woods?
-Guess so.

430
00:33:09,320 --> 00:33:11,160
Hey, Mintada. Where are you going?

431
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:25,280
What are you doing, Mintada?

432
00:33:31,320 --> 00:33:32,320
Mintada, you idiot.

433
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:34,240
We need to go help that girl.

434
00:33:34,320 --> 00:33:35,600
How do you know it's a girl?

435
00:33:38,520 --> 00:33:41,200
Oh, I get it now.

436
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:43,720
Are you coming?

437
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:48,560
Nah. You going alone
will probably be faster.

438
00:33:57,280 --> 00:33:59,880
Heading into the woods alone like this,
will he be alright?

439
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:03,440
Mintada grew up in the forest.

440
00:34:03,520 --> 00:34:07,760
No matter the forest, one walk through
and he knows every single tree.

441
00:34:32,159 --> 00:34:36,280
It's my fault. I was too tired and hungry

442
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:37,800
to keep an eye on Sa.

443
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:42,000
Me too.

444
00:34:43,199 --> 00:34:45,159
If anything happens to her,

445
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:48,159
what will we tell her parents?

446
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:52,159
Please stay calm.

447
00:34:52,719 --> 00:34:55,920
Every park ranger is doing their best.

448
00:34:56,600 --> 00:35:00,480
We'll work together
to bring your friend back safely.

449
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,560
Help me!

450
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:48,120
BEWARE OF WILD ELEPHANTS

451
00:36:17,320 --> 00:36:19,800
Should we pitch a tent for Mintada too?

452
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:21,040
No need.

453
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:23,960
A guy like Mintada…
If he hasn't found that girl yet,

454
00:36:24,040 --> 00:36:25,640
he won't be coming back to sleep.

455
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:29,240
You mean he's spending
the night in the forest?

456
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:30,680
No.

457
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:35,200
If he hasn't found her, even if it takes
all night, he won't stop searching.

458
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:44,120
Help me.

459
00:36:44,920 --> 00:36:46,360
I'm here.

460
00:36:46,440 --> 00:36:48,040
Help.

461
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:00,000
Help me.

462
00:37:48,040 --> 00:37:49,040
How is it going?

463
00:37:49,120 --> 00:37:52,000
The search team

464
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:54,480
checked all the trail routes

465
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:57,680
and nearby areas but found nothing.

466
00:37:57,760 --> 00:38:00,520
We think she might have wandered
deep into the forest by now.

467
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:03,200
We'll find Sa before it gets dark, right?

468
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:05,040
Dusk is falling,

469
00:38:05,120 --> 00:38:08,600
so we have to pause the search
and plan our next move.

470
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:12,000
Don't worry.

471
00:38:12,080 --> 00:38:15,400
We've coordinated with the military

472
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:17,840
for ground and air support.

473
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:20,000
Excuse me.
I need to head to a team meeting.

474
00:38:20,760 --> 00:38:22,160
Thank you very much.

475
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:26,720
No. Calm down.

476
00:38:28,600 --> 00:38:31,160
Professor, what are we going to do now?

477
00:38:32,760 --> 00:38:34,920
We'll have to inform her parents.

478
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:37,080
If Sa's parents find out,

479
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:40,200
we're all dead meat.

480
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:43,120
We still have to inform them regardless.

481
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:50,800
This shouldn't be happening.

482
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:56,000
Don't worry.

483
00:38:56,680 --> 00:38:59,720
My buddy Mintada went
into the woods to find your friend.

484
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:04,160
Mintada? A Kase student?

485
00:39:04,240 --> 00:39:05,360
Yes, Ma'am.

486
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:09,200
A real authentic Kase.

487
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:13,240
And how can you be so sure
he'll find our friend?

488
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:15,800
The Kase and the forest go hand in hand.

489
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:19,760
Trust me. My buddy
will definitely find your friend.

490
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:22,040
I'd bet my neck on it.

491
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:31,960
Hello. It's Pipach's residence.

492
00:39:36,760 --> 00:39:37,960
What?

493
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:42,440
Yes. I'll be right there!

494
00:39:45,560 --> 00:39:46,400
What happened?

495
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,160
Honey,

496
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:51,440
Sa is lost in the forest!

497
00:40:17,840 --> 00:40:19,120
An elephant sound!

498
00:40:31,080 --> 00:40:32,720
Don't make a sound.

499
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:34,640
Slowly step back.

500
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:37,720
Don't be afraid. I'm here to help you.

501
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:41,280
You. Hey, you!

502
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,520
Stop.

503
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:46,720
Stop right there. I said stop!

504
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:50,720
Why run from me?

505
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:52,000
Stay away!

506
00:40:55,960 --> 00:40:59,240
Trust me. I would never hurt you.

507
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:00,800
Stay back!

508
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:12,480
Have I met you somewhere before?

509
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:17,440
At the auditorium
during the international performance.

510
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:19,400
We go to the same uni.

511
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:24,880
Don't you remember?

512
00:41:32,200 --> 00:41:37,240
<i>Brothers and sisters</i>
<i>We eat fish, we protect the stream</i>

513
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:40,880
<i>Protect it, yes, protect it</i>

514
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:45,040
You are Kase.

515
00:41:52,840 --> 00:41:53,880
Yes.

516
00:41:54,640 --> 00:41:56,000
My name is Mintada.

517
00:41:57,560 --> 00:41:59,040
Mintada.

518
00:42:15,760 --> 00:42:18,360
Looks tasty. What is all this?

519
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:23,880
This one is fried salmon.
It's good for your eyes.

520
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:27,320
Cabbage soup, good for your eyes.

521
00:42:28,240 --> 00:42:33,160
And stir-fried morning glory,
also good for your eyes.

522
00:42:35,480 --> 00:42:36,560
All for eyesight, huh?

523
00:42:36,640 --> 00:42:40,000
Yep. Eat it all up.

524
00:42:40,080 --> 00:42:41,040
Okay.

525
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:52,600
Wow, so good!

526
00:42:52,680 --> 00:42:54,560
My vision is crystal clear now.

527
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:56,720
You're gorgeous.

528
00:42:58,280 --> 00:42:59,400
Look at you.

529
00:42:59,480 --> 00:43:00,480
Stop it.

530
00:43:01,040 --> 00:43:02,200
Truly gorgeous.

531
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,720
I know.

532
00:43:09,880 --> 00:43:11,640
Hello. It's Chonlachart.

533
00:43:13,160 --> 00:43:14,200
Yes, Aunt Sinee.

534
00:43:17,080 --> 00:43:20,480
Please calm down. I'm on my way. Goodbye.

535
00:43:23,600 --> 00:43:24,800
What is it, Chart?

536
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:27,080
Sa went to Khao Yai with her university

537
00:43:27,160 --> 00:43:28,800
and got lost. I have to leave right now.

538
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:30,000
Want me to go with you?

539
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:33,040
No, it's alright. As soon as
I have an update, I'll let you know.

540
00:43:34,440 --> 00:43:35,280
Okay.

541
00:43:50,720 --> 00:43:52,640
We'll spend the night here.

542
00:43:52,720 --> 00:43:55,800
Go sleep up on that tree stand.
I'll keep watch down here.

543
00:43:56,400 --> 00:43:59,520
What? Up there!

544
00:44:00,480 --> 00:44:02,920
No way. Take me out
of this forest right now.

545
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:06,480
We can't.
Waiting until morning is much safer.

546
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:09,360
No. I don't want to stay here anymore.

547
00:44:09,920 --> 00:44:11,000
Take me home!

548
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:12,520
Hey.

549
00:44:21,320 --> 00:44:24,120
You're exhausted and injured.
You won't make the trip right now.

550
00:44:24,200 --> 00:44:27,520
Yes I will!
I don't want to stay here anymore.

551
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:29,960
Don't you get it?
I want to leave as fast as possible.

552
00:44:30,040 --> 00:44:31,480
I don't want to stay here with--

553
00:44:34,200 --> 00:44:35,760
with some complete stranger.

554
00:44:38,360 --> 00:44:40,880
Can't you just
take me out of here right now?

555
00:44:40,960 --> 00:44:44,320
I want to go home.
I don't want to sleep up there.

556
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:46,480
Please?

557
00:44:48,640 --> 00:44:50,720
-What is it?
-A tiger's roar.

558
00:44:51,520 --> 00:44:52,480
Tiger?

559
00:44:54,120 --> 00:44:56,640
-Listen!
-Are you tricking me?

560
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:08,480
Get up there right now! Move!

561
00:45:12,520 --> 00:45:13,440
Let me help you.

562
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:55,840
Sit.

563
00:46:02,880 --> 00:46:04,440
Thanks, Mintada.

564
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:10,080
My name is Punpussa.

565
00:46:10,160 --> 00:46:12,200
Or you can call me just Sa.

566
00:46:13,080 --> 00:46:14,120
Just Sa.

567
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:19,640
No, it's not "just Sa". It's Sa.

568
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:26,320
Then, can I call you Pussa?

569
00:46:27,560 --> 00:46:28,680
Pussa?

570
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:31,200
That's kinda unique.

571
00:46:31,280 --> 00:46:33,920
Nobody has ever called me that before.

572
00:46:35,120 --> 00:46:36,520
Fine then. Pussa it is.

573
00:46:37,640 --> 00:46:39,680
Thanks, Pussa.

574
00:46:51,520 --> 00:46:54,240
Spirits of the forest and mountains,

575
00:46:54,320 --> 00:46:57,400
please keep my friend safe
and bring her back to us.

576
00:46:57,480 --> 00:46:59,520
Please hear our prayers.

577
00:47:00,400 --> 00:47:03,920
Who is in charge here?
I'll hold everyone fully accountable!

578
00:47:04,600 --> 00:47:05,720
Please calm down, honey.

579
00:47:05,800 --> 00:47:08,640
Calm down? Our daughter is missing.
This is huge!

580
00:47:09,480 --> 00:47:12,000
Making a scene won't solve anything.

581
00:47:13,760 --> 00:47:14,560
Hello.

582
00:47:14,640 --> 00:47:16,000
-Hello.
-Hello.

583
00:47:16,800 --> 00:47:20,160
How is Sa? How did she get lost,
Yoon, Nee?

584
00:47:20,240 --> 00:47:21,920
Tell me! What happened?!

585
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:24,360
-We're so sorry.
-We really have no idea.

586
00:47:25,360 --> 00:47:26,920
-I'm sorry.
-Hello.

587
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:28,720
Are you Punpussa' parents?

588
00:47:28,800 --> 00:47:31,560
-Yes! Tell me,
-Yes.

589
00:47:31,640 --> 00:47:34,760
how do you even operate here
to let my daughter disappear?

590
00:47:35,520 --> 00:47:39,320
We are doing our absolute best
to bring your daughter back safely.

591
00:47:39,400 --> 00:47:40,920
Doing your best?

592
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:44,040
You're sitting inside
instead of searching for my daughter.

593
00:47:44,120 --> 00:47:45,040
Calm down.

594
00:47:45,120 --> 00:47:46,840
I understand how you feel.

595
00:47:47,920 --> 00:47:49,280
Please rest assured

596
00:47:49,360 --> 00:47:53,200
that we will do everything possible
to bring your daughter back safe

597
00:47:53,280 --> 00:47:54,360
as soon as possible.

598
00:47:55,800 --> 00:48:00,080
Ma'am, Sir, nobody wanted
an incident like this to occur.

599
00:48:00,160 --> 00:48:01,480
Please try to stay calm.

600
00:48:02,520 --> 00:48:04,400
Yes, I understand.

601
00:48:54,440 --> 00:48:57,200
Looks like Mintada won't be back tonight.

602
00:48:58,480 --> 00:48:59,640
He's not coming back.

603
00:48:59,720 --> 00:49:02,880
I heard Kase people

604
00:49:02,960 --> 00:49:05,320
can trek the forest day and night.

605
00:49:05,840 --> 00:49:06,960
Was I wrong?

606
00:49:07,040 --> 00:49:09,000
You heard right.

607
00:49:09,520 --> 00:49:11,960
If Mintada wanted to return now, he could.

608
00:49:12,480 --> 00:49:15,360
But he isn't coming back
because he doesn't want to.

609
00:49:16,760 --> 00:49:19,640
Doesn't want to? Care to translate that?

610
00:49:20,560 --> 00:49:23,920
Maybe this is the night
he's been waiting for all along.

611
00:50:29,880 --> 00:50:30,960
Mintada.

612
00:50:32,160 --> 00:50:34,600
Have you been sitting here
without sleeping all night?

613
00:50:40,200 --> 00:50:42,160
-Thank you.
-Sure.

614
00:50:44,800 --> 00:50:47,360
How's your ankle feeling?
Has the pain gone away?

615
00:50:49,680 --> 00:50:52,440
It's much better now.
I'm ready to hit the trail again.

616
00:50:59,760 --> 00:51:00,920
So…

617
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:04,560
You can really get me
out of this forest, right?

618
00:51:06,280 --> 00:51:07,120
Yes.

619
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:28,320
Are we heading out right now?

620
00:51:28,960 --> 00:51:29,880
Yes.

621
00:51:40,440 --> 00:51:42,760
Everyone must be waiting for you by now.

622
00:51:56,080 --> 00:51:56,920
Uncle Pipach. Aunt Pisinee.

623
00:51:57,760 --> 00:51:58,600
-Chart!
-Chart.

624
00:51:58,680 --> 00:52:00,160
-Hello.
-Hello.

625
00:52:00,240 --> 00:52:01,440
Any updates or progress yet?

626
00:52:01,520 --> 00:52:04,520
The search team left this morning
but who knows when they'll find her.

627
00:52:04,600 --> 00:52:06,040
I'll join the search right now.

628
00:52:06,120 --> 00:52:08,480
But Chart, you drove all night.
Are you going to be okay?

629
00:52:08,560 --> 00:52:11,760
I can handle even more. I just need
a quick splash of water on my face.

630
00:52:26,080 --> 00:52:27,240
Wash your face first.

631
00:52:32,680 --> 00:52:33,840
It's ice-cold!

632
00:52:40,680 --> 00:52:43,360
Is this water safe to drink?

633
00:52:43,960 --> 00:52:45,440
Yes, it's clean.

634
00:52:52,400 --> 00:52:53,280
Here.

635
00:53:04,280 --> 00:53:05,560
So refreshing!

636
00:53:07,040 --> 00:53:09,640
How did you know there was a stream here?

637
00:53:09,720 --> 00:53:11,040
I grew up in the forest.

638
00:53:11,840 --> 00:53:14,960
Forest terrain always slopes
toward water sources.

639
00:53:17,640 --> 00:53:18,480
You're amazing!

640
00:53:19,160 --> 00:53:23,240
It's nothing special.
City people know the city.

641
00:53:23,320 --> 00:53:25,920
Forest people know the forest.

642
00:53:32,840 --> 00:53:36,040
How much further until we get out of here?

643
00:53:37,160 --> 00:53:38,480
Not much further now.

644
00:53:51,640 --> 00:53:53,280
Wait, Mintada.

645
00:53:55,640 --> 00:53:58,440
Your definition of "not far"
is totally different from mine.

646
00:54:00,240 --> 00:54:03,320
You're power-walking
like you're in a speed-walking race!

647
00:54:03,400 --> 00:54:07,040
Seriously, do you normally walk this fast?

648
00:54:07,960 --> 00:54:11,200
I'm sorry. I thought you were
in a hurry to get out of the forest.

649
00:54:11,280 --> 00:54:13,720
It doesn't need to be this fast.

650
00:54:14,560 --> 00:54:16,440
Okay. Then, have some water.

651
00:54:21,040 --> 00:54:22,080
Thank you.

652
00:54:36,840 --> 00:54:39,320
I drank all your water. I'm sorry.

653
00:54:39,400 --> 00:54:42,640
It's alright. We're not far now.

654
00:54:42,720 --> 00:54:45,160
"Not far" again?

655
00:54:45,920 --> 00:54:47,720
It really isn't far now.

656
00:54:47,800 --> 00:54:50,360
Let's keep moving. I'll slow down.

657
00:54:50,440 --> 00:54:54,000
And you speed up a bit.
We'll walk side-by-side.

658
00:54:55,560 --> 00:54:56,480
Let's go.

659
00:55:04,600 --> 00:55:05,680
Thank you very much.

660
00:55:07,160 --> 00:55:08,400
<i>Calling base.</i>

661
00:55:10,520 --> 00:55:13,120
<i>Regarding the missing student</i>
<i>from yesterday,</i>

662
00:55:13,200 --> 00:55:15,200
<i>mission complete.</i>

663
00:55:15,760 --> 00:55:18,440
<i>We are bringing</i>
<i>the student out of the forest.</i>

664
00:55:18,520 --> 00:55:19,880
Copy that.

665
00:55:19,960 --> 00:55:20,960
We found her.

666
00:55:23,160 --> 00:55:24,720
Honey, Sa is back!

667
00:55:25,520 --> 00:55:27,120
Chart, we found her.

668
00:55:27,200 --> 00:55:28,560
Thank you very much.

669
00:55:28,640 --> 00:55:30,160
Thank you very much.

670
00:55:43,360 --> 00:55:45,280
-Sa!
-Sa!

671
00:55:45,360 --> 00:55:47,160
-Yoon. Nee.
-Sa!

672
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:50,480
Sa, how are you feeling?

673
00:55:50,560 --> 00:55:52,800
I was so worried!
I couldn't eat single thing!

674
00:55:54,120 --> 00:55:55,400
Sa!

675
00:55:55,480 --> 00:55:56,760
Chart!

676
00:55:57,440 --> 00:55:58,680
-Sa!
-Mom.

677
00:55:58,760 --> 00:56:00,120
-Dad.
-Sa, are you alright?

678
00:56:00,640 --> 00:56:04,240
Sa, sweetheart!
Are you hurt or in pain anywhere?

679
00:56:05,320 --> 00:56:06,240
Hey!

680
00:56:07,720 --> 00:56:11,000
-You're awesome, man!
-Told you. This guy is no ordinary person.

681
00:56:13,360 --> 00:56:15,120
Ah, Mintada!

682
00:56:15,200 --> 00:56:16,120
Mintada!

683
00:56:16,200 --> 00:56:17,320
Are you safe, sweetie?

684
00:56:17,400 --> 00:56:20,880
I'm safe and sound, Dad.
Someone helped get me out.

685
00:56:20,960 --> 00:56:22,040
Who helped you out?

686
00:56:22,760 --> 00:56:25,000
His name is Mintada. He's standing over--

687
00:56:27,400 --> 00:56:28,600
Where did he go?

688
00:56:28,680 --> 00:56:30,520
He probably went to get some rest.

689
00:56:31,400 --> 00:56:32,760
You need to rest too.

690
00:56:32,840 --> 00:56:35,520
Go clean up, shower,
and then we're heading home.

691
00:56:35,600 --> 00:56:36,840
You're taking her home now?

692
00:56:36,920 --> 00:56:39,760
Yes. I am definitely not letting
my daughter stay here any longer.

693
00:56:39,840 --> 00:56:41,480
Very well. Right this way please.

694
00:56:41,560 --> 00:56:42,440
-Let's go.
-This way.

695
00:56:44,880 --> 00:56:45,960
-Come on, kids.
-Let's go.

696
00:56:46,040 --> 00:56:47,280
Honey, let's go.

697
00:56:54,000 --> 00:56:57,720
Our daughter and that Kase guy
seem a bit too close.

698
00:56:57,800 --> 00:57:00,160
Mintada, this is Chart.

699
00:57:00,760 --> 00:57:01,680
This is Mintada.

700
00:57:01,760 --> 00:57:02,880
Hello.

701
00:57:02,960 --> 00:57:04,800
I finally get to meet you in person.

702
00:57:04,880 --> 00:57:06,480
Mintada.

703
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:08,840
I'm sure this money
is worth a great deal to you.

704
00:57:08,920 --> 00:57:11,480
The Kase live in poverty

705
00:57:11,560 --> 00:57:13,280
and have no land of their own.

706
00:57:13,360 --> 00:57:14,280
That's not true!

707
00:57:14,360 --> 00:57:16,360
<i>I was wrong,</i>
<i>not to believe you from the start</i>

708
00:57:16,440 --> 00:57:17,960
that we live in different worlds.

709
00:57:18,040 --> 00:57:20,000
<i>Just as Colonel Layee said.</i>

710
00:57:20,080 --> 00:57:21,040
Blood must be paid with blood.

711
00:57:24,320 --> 00:57:25,680
-Pussa, Pussa.
-Sa!

712
00:58:02,920 --> 00:58:05,000
Subtitle translation by:
Onamon Chaipramote
